To make changes to the Secure Boot UEFI variables, the system needs to be in
Secure Boot setup mode. In this mode, Secure Boot itself is disabled and the
variable holding the Platform Key has been wiped.

To activate setup mode, you need to enter your motherboard's firmware
(sometimes called BIOS) and delete the Platform Key.
Look for options similar to:
    - Key Management
    - Secure Boot Custom Mode
    - Clear Platform Key
    - Delete PK
    - Delete all Secure Boot variables

We will populate all Secure Boot variables, so if your motherboard has no
option for just deleting the Platform Key, deleting all Secure Boot
variables/keys is also fine.

After rebooting, run
%1 10
or
%1 secureboot
to re-run the current step. To boot directly into the firmware, you can run:
systemctl reboot --firmware-setup
